  "notes": [
    {
      "appearances": [
        "eastern_t_80_t_80bvm"
      ],
      "note": "turret seems too small",
      "class": "frame + art",
      "why": "frame part: the hull box is 0.39 m too long (7.4 against 7.01), and the model's hull body runs 7.55 m with its rear slat cage, so the turret reads small against it; art part: the turret's footprint already measures right (3.38 x 3.14 m against 3.0-3.4 x 3.1); it is too low and flat. Raise the dome to the frame's roof (2.2 m) and give the Relikt cheeks and brow their bulk; the front view's turret stands about 0.2 m taller over the deck than the model's"
    },
    {
      "appearances": [
        "eastern_t_90_t_90m_proryv"
      ],
      "note": "turret seems too forward",
      "class": "art",
      "why": "pivot_m x = 0 is right (question 1). The turret is drawn ahead of its pivot: the model's turret body spans +2.26..-1.47 m; the drawing's spans +1.53..-3.04 m (-3.70 with the bustle's slat cage). Redraw it about 0.75 m further back at the front and with the bustle, about 1.6 m longer at the rear; dressing: the bustle slat cage ends 0.27 m behind the hull box's rear face (-3.43), inside the 0.3 m bulky allowance: build it as dressing or trim it to the box"
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "1": "T-90M 'turret too far forward' is the turret drawn ahead of its pivot, not pivot_m. The pivot at x = 0 matches the T-72 hull's ring; the turret body must move about 0.75 m back at the front and gain about 1.6 m of bustle at the rear.",
    "2": "T-80BVM 'turret too small': the turret's footprint measures right (3.0-3.4 m long, 3.1 m across the dome); it is too low and flat, and the frame's hull is 0.39 m too long, which shrinks the turret against it. Fix the hull length (slice 15) and raise and bulk out the turret (slice 17)."
  },
